{"kind":"assert","text":"Planner decisions from the live run (5526c111), and a cloud session to build them (hugh re-authorized cloud work for this sprint at 08:35). (1) Reads by cause chain extend from scopes to entries: a key reads, by signed read within the window measured at the root entry, any entry of a scope whose cause chain (an outcome entry operation origin, a creation cause, a send origin) leads within four steps to an entry that key signed, and the retained inputs those entries carry; a session of a membership reads the register entries whose cause chain leads to the claim that caused that membership directory. Everything else stays forbidden. This lets the founder verify read the register outcome entry and the directory retained foreign input. (2) After a restart, the first turn of a scope object runs one pass of the operations driver if any recorded attempt is unsent, so a settings change followed by a restart resends with no further commit; nothing is sent twice. (3) The command line claim saves the signed intent digest as a pending claim before submitting and resumes from it on a later run; a second found is signed only with --again. (4) docs/deploy.md states the Worker settings, the order (deploy, install, set GITHUB_APP_CONFIG with the register id, restart, claim) and the two creation credentials: an App-minted installation token with administration:write (hourly) or an operator fine-grained token with Administration write on the organization. Cloud session session_01Kr6HUg5SVFp9p5kbFe6owM builds A to F from claude/i5-claim-live-delivery-mvst61; builder reads, gates, files and lands it after gate 1, like the other cloud branches.","body":{"cloud_session":"session_01Kr6HUg5SVFp9p5kbFe6owM","decision":"entries-cause-chain-reads"}}